    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĕnē-plăcĕo</span></b> ,
			ŭi, ĭtum, 2, v. n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to</i>
			
			<i>please</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1
					Cor. 16, 2</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>P. a.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĕnēplăcĭtus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>pleasing</i>, <i>acceptable</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Ecclus. 34, 21</span></i>; Ambros. lsaac et An. 7, 57 <i>init.</i>—As <i>subst.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĕnē-plăcĭtum</span></b> ,
				i, n., <i>good
			pleasure</i>, <i>gracious purpose</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Eph. 1,
				9</span></i> et saep.</div>
